        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "All reactions were routinely conducted under inert atmosphere. 1.72 g (1.41 mmol) of La3(OtBu)9(HOtBu)2 dissolved in 15 ml of toluene were refluxed for over 9 h. The solution was evaporated in vacuo leaving an off-white powder which was recrystallised in THF, giving 1.40 g (55%) of La5O(OtBu)13 (1) as colourless crystals. Suitable crystals of 1 for X-ray diffraction were obtained from THF solutions as a bis(THF) solvate. The discussion also notes reflux of La3(OtBu)9(tBuOH)2 in toluene for 6 h afforded 1 by crystallisation.",
        "reagents": [
          {
            "name": "La3(OtBu)9(HOtBu)2",
